  "Question": "Why does a carpenter need to fix only two points when snapping an ink line?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "The perpendicular segment is the shortest",
    "B": "Two points determine a line",
    "C": "The line segment between two points is the shortest path",
    "D": "Through a point outside a line, there is exactly one line parallel to the given line"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Once two points of the ink line are fixed, there is only one line passing through them, so its position is determined. This is based on the fact that “two points determine a line.”",
